# .gitignore of a code repository.
#
# This file is the reference on the versioned / local boundary — a folder's name decides nothing,
# only this file does. Every entry, or group of entries, says why it is here.
#
# ⚠ Build artefacts are deliberately absent. The test for an ignore rule is not whether it is
# anchored but whether it can ever be **wrong**, and a rule posted in advance for a stack this
# repository does not yet use is a decision taken about cases nobody has seen. Observed: a `dist/`
# rule, added to an empty section, silently swallowed a vendored library folder several levels
# down — nothing failed, nothing was reported, and the clone on the other side would simply not
# have built. Add each rule when its artefact appears, anchored to where it appears.
#
# The costs are not symmetric: a file wrongly ignored is invisible, a file wrongly tracked is
# obvious immediately.

# ── Editor tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Machine-local settings. The editor workspace file lives at the corpus root and belongs to no
# repository.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace

# ── Temporary files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
~$*
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp
*~

# ── System ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ── Local, unshared work ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scratch files and throwaway experiments. The folder exists so there is somewhere to put one
# without wondering whether it should be versioned: by construction, the answer is no.
_local/
